			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824773">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror, Drama/Emotional.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> 2 plush puppies that come to life whenever a child is nearby. They act like regular puppies, but very aggressive towards any adult with a lab coat. They have no way of harming anyone.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The puppies have the consciousness of 2 young kids. The kids and one of their parents were on the brink of death after an accident. While in the hospital, a doctor was testing to see if they could transfer consciousness into anything other than a computer, and used the family as test subjects. It is implied that the near-dead parent is somewhere, but has gone missing. The 2 kids are all the Foundation has so far.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I intend this to be a slow burn, of sorts. The final addendum will reveal the full story, but before that, there are clues. The pups will be afraid of the researchers and would try to protect any kid from them, one will react to their human name, they'll try to get people they trust to follow them somewhere, etc. It's a little mystery before the end of the article.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> While the pups wouldn't be able to talk, I am thinking about having an &quot;interview&quot; log of sorts, where they'd be able to point to words on a board and communicate that way. I'm not sure if that's a good idea though, so any insight will help with that!</p>

